`x + 10#u32`, the tactic `step` finds a specification of `e` among the theorems
tagged `@[step]`, tries to prove its precondition, which it
leaves as a goal if it cannot, and introduces the
result of `e` together with its postcondition. The clause `as ⟨ res, hres ⟩`
names the result and its postcondition. Here the specification of the addition
gives `hres : res.val = x.val + 10`.
